Yes, the -1, 0 and 1 are the values at which the simple slopes will be estimated. You don't have to use -1, 0, and 1 but they are the defaults. If you're using a fixed factor methods of scale setting (fixing latent variances to 1 and latent means to 0) then this provides estimates at 1 SD before the mean, the mean, and 1 SD above the mean for the moderator. If you're using another method of scale setting, it is important to examine simple slopes at meaningful values for the moderator.

Alex

